{# Response for an inspector edit: the whole graph (morphed into #graph) plus an
   out-of-band refresh of #inspector so the panel reflects the saved server state.

   The OOB swap MUST use a morph style, because hx-ext="morph" makes the idiomorph
   extension intercept every OOB swap; its isInlineSwap() crashes on non-morph
   styles like "innerHTML". "morph" (outerHTML) also avoids the swapStyle:selector
   colon clash in the hx-swap-oob syntax, so the <aside> tag must match the real
   element so its outerHTML morphs cleanly in place. #}
{% include "_graph.njk" %}
<aside id="inspector" hx-swap-oob="morph">
{% include "_inspector.njk" %}
</aside>
